# Everything the console build does not read.
#
# The deployed artefact is a static build of `sentry/console`, which touches
# only that directory and the recording committed inside its `public/`. The
# control plane, the kernel agent, the reference estate and the design set stay
# in the repository — they are the project — but uploading them to a build that
# cannot use them only slows the deploy and gives framework detection more to
# be wrong about.

design/
.github/

sentry/agent/
sentry/api/
sentry/core/
sentry/worker/
sentry/estate/
sentry/deploy/
sentry/tools/
sentry/contracts/

# A downloaded copy of this repository that sits in the working tree. Untracked,
# so it never reaches GitHub — but a CLI deploy uploads the directory, not the
# commit, and this would go with it.
sentry-main/

.DS_Store
.claude/
